    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey my bosch dishwasher is showing an E15 error code and wont start. i looked at the manual but i'm not sure what to do first. how do i check the leak sensor and how can i dry out the bottom of the machine if there's water stuck down there?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "An E15 error on a Bosch dishwasher typically indicates a drainage issue or a blocked drain augmenter valve, rather than necessarily a faulty sensor. You should first check that the drain filter hasn't become clogged with debris or that the drain hose is kinked or disconnected. Once you clear any visible blockages, running the \"Rinse Aid\" or \"DrawOut\" cycle manually often drains the remaining standing water from the bottom of the machine without an empty run cycle. If the problem persists after clearing the drain and running the drawout cycle, it likely points to a malfunctioning drain valve or hose, which usually requires professional service.",
