    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i tried cleaning the filter but it didn't help. i think i definitely have water sitting in the pan at the very bottom underneath everything. how do i actually get to that sensor to see if it's triggered? and is there a way to dry it out without taking the whole thing apart or something? it just feels like there's water stuck in a place i can't reach.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To access the bottom drain sensor, you typically need to lift the entire rack assembly and lean elbow-deep into the dish caddy, where the “check level” switch is located just below the sump area. While there is no safe, quick method to completely dry out the sump without accessing the machine, you can try placing a large bowl in the front of the open door and pouring hot water in to evaporate some moisture, followed by running a short \"Draw Out\" cycle if your model supports it. If the water remains or the error persists, the sensor is likely triggered and needs to be manually pressed while running that cycle, but if the tank is full, this DIY approach won't work.",
