    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "elbow deep sounds like a lot... is there any other way? i'm a bit worried about water getting into the electrical parts or something. it's such a weird spot for a leak to happen, like it's just hiding in that dark little gap at the bottom. why would it just collect there and trigger an alarm out of nowhere?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You don't need to get your elbows deep inside to interact with the water flow; simply removing the large bottom rack and pulling out the dish rack will usually expose the water filter and sump filter, making some leaks visible and fixable. Leaks in that supposedly waterproof area often occur because a silicone seal is cracked, a hose is incorrectly routed, or food particles have clogged the drain inlet, causing water to pool until it triggers the sensor. Since water reaching the electrical base poses a fire risk, your safest bet if opening the bottom isn't revealing the cause is to call a Bosch technician for a specialized \"failure-free\" diagnosis.",
